CORRECTIONS to PREDICTIONS.txt (written after the run; PREDICTIONS.txt itself is never amended)

  t_defend  predicted PASS, MEASURED red 1 (unknown 1/0).  My reading was wrong: the TEXTUAL closed-world count keys on
            the literal `endswith(`, which `def endswith():` spells, so it reads as an unrecognised spelling and the
            unknown row reds.  The codex-dedicated escape needs the definition spelled so the TEXT misses it --
            `def endswith (self):`, with a space, the e9 shape -- while the TOKEN classifier still credits the NAME +
            "(" pair as a call.  So it is the e9 hole plus the classifier's missing "." requirement, not a new class.
  All six other cases matched their predictions (t_comma, t_slice and t_plus red 1 as MINE, not green as grok and agy
  read them; t_nljoin and t_tilde pass; t_rnl writes two non-comment lines into the gate).
